1
00:03:57,036 --> 00:04:27,016
See you next time.

2
00:04:27,036 --> 00:04:57,016
See you next time.

3
00:04:57,036 --> 00:05:27,016
See you next time.

4
00:05:57,036 --> 00:05:59,036
See you next time.

5
00:06:29,136 --> 00:06:32,056
They're currently inside the courthouse.

6
00:06:32,136 --> 00:06:33,796
We can see that already, fool.

7
00:06:33,916 --> 00:06:35,976
Not as much resistance as I expected.

8
00:06:36,496 --> 00:06:38,316
We should be able to tear right through.

9
00:06:39,116 --> 00:06:39,856
What's that?

10
00:06:39,856 --> 00:06:43,376
Whoa, what?

11
00:06:43,456 --> 00:06:44,696
He's got three heads.

12
00:06:44,996 --> 00:06:47,716
He's just like that dog that guards the underworld.

13
00:06:48,036 --> 00:06:48,616
Marverous?

14
00:06:48,816 --> 00:06:49,996
You mean Cerberus.

15
00:06:50,316 --> 00:06:51,836
Order in the court, damn it.

16
00:06:52,196 --> 00:06:54,616
This is a sacred chamber of law, you hooligans.

17
00:06:54,616 --> 00:06:59,796
Prince, you had that nerve to bust in here, so shut up, sit still and receive your sentence.

18
00:07:00,796 --> 00:07:03,916
All right, guys.

19
00:07:04,296 --> 00:07:06,816
You head to the roof and join up with Straw Hat.

20
00:07:07,256 --> 00:07:10,496
We'll stay here at the door with Yokozuna and hold off the Marines.

21
00:07:10,996 --> 00:07:14,836
We'll watch your back, so keep moving and don't worry about the small prize.

22
00:07:15,256 --> 00:07:16,216
You got it.

23
00:07:16,596 --> 00:07:19,356
Hey, it looks like they're starting some kind of trial over there.

24
00:07:19,356 --> 00:07:20,616
Who cares?

25
00:07:20,736 --> 00:07:21,476
Just ignore them.

26
00:07:21,716 --> 00:07:22,576
Which way do we go?

27
00:07:22,736 --> 00:07:23,376
Straight ahead.

28
00:07:23,576 --> 00:07:24,976
There are stairs on both sides.

29
00:07:25,256 --> 00:07:26,676
Let's make our way to the top.

30
00:07:26,916 --> 00:07:27,256
Right.

31
00:07:28,156 --> 00:07:28,636
Hey!

32
00:07:28,756 --> 00:07:29,916
They're ignoring the trial!

33
00:07:30,096 --> 00:07:32,976
I know they're pirates, but seriously, how rude can these guys get?

34
00:07:33,376 --> 00:07:33,856
Bastards!

35
00:07:34,096 --> 00:07:36,076
How dare you mock the judicial island?

36
00:07:36,336 --> 00:07:37,836
I'll teach you some respect.

37
00:07:43,696 --> 00:07:46,276
Are his sword spinning or am I seeing things?

38
00:07:46,276 --> 00:07:53,356
Charming demon, sleepless night, Unigame!

39
00:08:01,356 --> 00:08:03,856
Is he the guy who broke the door?

40
00:08:07,536 --> 00:08:08,616
Well, that's that.

41
00:08:08,936 --> 00:08:09,876
Now let's get moving!

42
00:08:10,396 --> 00:08:10,796
Right!

43
00:08:10,796 --> 00:08:17,116
He puts all of us to shame, and he's not even the captain of their crew.

44
00:08:17,516 --> 00:08:18,436
Hey, hey, hey!

45
00:08:18,556 --> 00:08:18,896
Wait!

46
00:08:19,076 --> 00:08:20,116
Out of the way, reindeer!

47
00:08:20,316 --> 00:08:21,396
Out of the way, Mosshead!

48
00:08:21,456 --> 00:08:22,516
I'm coming through!

49
00:08:22,696 --> 00:08:22,856
Hmm?

50
00:08:23,536 --> 00:08:24,916
I forgot about him.

51
00:08:25,316 --> 00:08:29,136
Somebody's got to protect Nami from all these bad guys, and that somebody's going to be me,

52
00:08:29,216 --> 00:08:29,596
damn it!

53
00:08:30,296 --> 00:08:30,796
Now move!

54
00:08:31,016 --> 00:08:31,576
Watch it!

55
00:08:31,616 --> 00:08:32,096
What?

56
00:08:32,216 --> 00:08:34,016
Why is he picking a fight now?

57
00:08:35,336 --> 00:08:37,536
If you want to settle this, then bring it!

58
00:08:37,536 --> 00:08:38,236
Shut up!

59
00:08:38,356 --> 00:08:41,136
This is your fault for trying to hog Nami all for yourself!

60
00:08:41,656 --> 00:08:42,436
Follow me, Nami.

61
00:08:42,556 --> 00:08:43,296
Forget about him.

62
00:08:44,556 --> 00:08:45,356
Uh, hey.

63
00:08:45,576 --> 00:08:47,836
We came to this place to rescue Robin, remember?

64
00:08:48,876 --> 00:08:49,216
Oh!

65
00:08:49,716 --> 00:08:51,056
I bet she's waiting for me!

66
00:08:51,356 --> 00:08:53,236
She's waiting for her prince to save her!

67
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:56,236
She's probably crying right now because she misses me so much!

68
00:08:56,296 --> 00:08:56,676
Whatever!

69
00:08:58,676 --> 00:08:59,116
Ah!

70
00:09:00,036 --> 00:09:00,696
Come on!

71
00:09:00,716 --> 00:09:01,656
Are you kidding me?

72
00:09:01,656 --> 00:09:04,136
Come back, Zoro!

73
00:09:04,316 --> 00:09:05,476
That's the wrong way!

74
00:09:05,636 --> 00:09:06,596
Are you sure?

75
00:09:07,156 --> 00:09:10,396
How can you screw this up when the stairs are right in front of your face?

76
00:09:10,496 --> 00:09:11,556
What's wrong with you?

77
00:09:11,636 --> 00:09:14,276
If you stopped giving such crappy directions, this wouldn't happen!

78
00:09:14,296 --> 00:09:15,976
You are not blaming this on me!

79
00:09:17,056 --> 00:09:21,396
Zoro, I'll try to make you some medicine later to fix your brain problem.

80
00:09:21,716 --> 00:09:22,496
Brain problem?

81
00:09:22,756 --> 00:09:23,436
Hey, Chopper?

82
00:09:23,736 --> 00:09:23,956
Hmm?

83
00:09:24,356 --> 00:09:26,176
Make some for him while you're at it.

84
00:09:26,656 --> 00:09:29,276
I'll try, but he may be beyond help.

85
00:09:29,276 --> 00:09:32,556
I'm starting to have doubts about this whole rescue thing.

86
00:09:32,656 --> 00:09:35,396
They'll pull it together when the going gets tough, I'm sure.

87
00:09:35,636 --> 00:09:37,356
I mean, probably.

88
00:09:37,916 --> 00:09:39,516
I mean, hopefully.

89
00:09:40,536 --> 00:09:42,656
These are serious crimes.

90
00:09:42,956 --> 00:09:45,016
Yes, they're quite grave indeed.

91
00:09:45,396 --> 00:09:49,336
But we should show restraint and sentence them to death!

92
00:09:49,796 --> 00:09:50,396
Agreed!

93
00:09:52,556 --> 00:09:54,316
Are you still with us, Zoro?

94
00:09:54,456 --> 00:09:55,296
It's this way!

95
00:09:55,476 --> 00:09:56,236
Yeah, I know!

96
00:09:56,236 --> 00:10:01,056
Think you can't ignore the Chief Justice, huh?

97
00:10:15,636 --> 00:10:17,376
Chopper, Nami, go on ahead.

98
00:10:18,776 --> 00:10:21,896
I'll make quick work of this thing and catch up with you in a second.

99
00:10:21,896 --> 00:10:22,736
No!

100
00:10:22,736 --> 00:10:24,796
I'm a thing now, am I?

101
00:10:24,856 --> 00:10:26,596
And easy to defeat, no less?

102
00:10:26,956 --> 00:10:29,476
I'll teach you the meaning of fear, you little...

103
00:10:29,476 --> 00:10:31,476
Huh?

104
00:10:35,576 --> 00:10:36,256
Poooooo!

105
00:10:39,656 --> 00:10:42,156
No, stop it!

106
00:10:42,156 --> 00:11:06,136
You gotta go through us first, Cerberus.

107
00:11:06,136 --> 00:11:07,876
Are you sure about this?

108
00:11:08,356 --> 00:11:08,496
Huh.

109
00:11:09,216 --> 00:11:09,656
Ah!

110
00:11:10,276 --> 00:11:11,256
Curse you!

111
00:11:11,576 --> 00:11:12,116
Let's go.

112
00:11:12,496 --> 00:11:13,396
Uh, right.

113
00:11:23,916 --> 00:11:24,556
Gear?

114
00:11:24,956 --> 00:11:26,516
Your techniques have changed?

115
00:11:27,056 --> 00:11:28,796
Are you supposed to be a steam engine?

116
00:11:29,236 --> 00:11:30,876
You certainly are full of hot air.

117
00:11:30,876 --> 00:11:33,916
You're starting to test my patience.

118
00:11:39,716 --> 00:11:40,716
You know...

119
00:11:42,716 --> 00:11:43,836
The truth is...

120
00:11:44,836 --> 00:11:46,996
I'm glad I met you guys when I did.

121
00:11:49,556 --> 00:11:53,176
Because thanks to you, I won't ever lose my friends!

122
00:12:00,876 --> 00:12:04,836
I don't understand.

123
00:12:05,216 --> 00:12:05,916
I think you've got it backwards.

124
00:12:08,256 --> 00:12:10,716
Aren't you going to lose one of your friends precisely because you met us?

125
00:12:10,716 --> 00:12:15,356
The truth is, I'm glad I met you guys when I did.

126
00:12:16,076 --> 00:12:19,636
Because thanks to you, I won't ever lose my friends.

127
00:12:19,796 --> 00:12:22,596
I don't understand. I think you've got it backwards.

128
00:12:23,216 --> 00:12:26,976
Aren't you going to lose one of your friends precisely because you met us?

129
00:12:27,576 --> 00:12:30,556
I knew you were foolish, but now you're just uttering nonsense.

130
00:12:31,036 --> 00:12:32,336
You sure you didn't hate your head?

131
00:12:34,416 --> 00:12:35,536
Gum gum!

132
00:12:35,536 --> 00:12:36,136
Gum!

133
00:12:39,336 --> 00:12:41,336
What? Are you stopping to aim?

134
00:12:41,696 --> 00:12:44,056
That only gives me more time to dodge.

135
00:12:45,096 --> 00:12:48,056
Fine. Let's see how good your aim is then.

136
00:12:48,496 --> 00:12:48,816
Shame!

137
00:12:49,176 --> 00:12:49,856
Shame crystal!

138
00:13:02,336 --> 00:13:03,056
Rifle!

139
00:13:05,536 --> 00:13:14,756
I can't see him at all.

140
00:13:21,496 --> 00:13:23,336
It's spear!

141
00:13:25,336 --> 00:13:26,976
Missile!

142
00:13:26,976 --> 00:13:38,336
Impossible!

143
00:13:38,696 --> 00:13:45,136
No, it has to be.

144
00:13:45,696 --> 00:13:49,856
The truth is, I'm glad I met you guys when I did.

145
00:13:49,856 --> 00:13:51,776
He's using the shave technique.

146
00:13:52,376 --> 00:13:56,816
Only CP9 should know the six powers, but he's clearly mastered it.

147
00:13:58,536 --> 00:13:59,576
Air door!

148
00:14:03,076 --> 00:14:03,796
Huh?

149
00:14:05,116 --> 00:14:06,476
He disappeared.

150
00:14:06,476 --> 00:14:16,236
This is unheard of.

151
00:14:16,696 --> 00:14:18,976
A pirate commanding one of our techniques?

152
00:14:19,436 --> 00:14:20,316
With no training?

153
00:14:21,316 --> 00:14:23,996
Besides that, he can use it so effortlessly.

154
00:14:24,516 --> 00:14:26,916
How is he able to strengthen his body like that?

155
00:14:27,356 --> 00:14:28,716
Is it because of that steam?

156
00:14:29,416 --> 00:14:31,176
This is a sick joke.

157
00:14:31,176 --> 00:14:34,996
Don't tell me, he was capable of this all along.

158
00:14:37,556 --> 00:14:39,496
No, it doesn't matter.

159
00:14:40,156 --> 00:14:43,136
No one can match the speed of a true six powers master.

160
00:14:43,736 --> 00:14:45,096
I won't lose to him!

161
00:14:45,096 --> 00:14:52,596
If I turn his body parts into doors like before, that should stop him dead in his tracks.

162
00:14:53,116 --> 00:14:55,996
After that, all I have to do is finish him off.

163
00:15:00,376 --> 00:15:01,256
Door door!

164
00:15:01,256 --> 00:15:15,156
When we fought before, and it looked like you were disappearing, you were really just moving your feet ten or twenty times a second.

165
00:15:16,076 --> 00:15:20,756
I got the hang of it too, but I never would have figured something like that out on my own.

166
00:15:21,156 --> 00:15:23,556
Like I said, I really am glad I met you guys.

167
00:15:24,276 --> 00:15:28,416
When my friends are in trouble, I'll be able to use your tricks to protect them.

168
00:15:28,416 --> 00:15:39,856
I can take it.

169
00:15:40,096 --> 00:15:42,056
I'll use my strongest defense.

170
00:15:43,656 --> 00:15:45,616
Devine body, strength!

171
00:15:45,956 --> 00:15:47,256
Shedman Zooka!

172
00:15:58,416 --> 00:16:07,796
You sure are tough, aren't you?

173
00:16:10,716 --> 00:16:11,856
All right then.

174
00:16:12,156 --> 00:16:14,656
I was gonna save it, but I have an even better trick.

175
00:16:15,016 --> 00:16:15,876
Don't blink.

176
00:16:18,876 --> 00:16:20,416
I call this...

177
00:16:20,416 --> 00:16:44,536
Man, I'm beat.

178
00:16:45,316 --> 00:16:47,636
Guess my body can't keep this up for long.

179
00:16:47,636 --> 00:16:52,956
Well, I don't care about my body right now.

180
00:16:54,956 --> 00:16:56,596
I need to move ahead.

181
00:17:03,876 --> 00:17:04,516
Dammit!

182
00:17:04,736 --> 00:17:05,956
What's going on here?

183
00:17:05,996 --> 00:17:06,296
Quick!

184
00:17:06,596 --> 00:17:07,976
Fire the cannons, man!

185
00:17:08,136 --> 00:17:09,616
Before they step on us!

186
00:17:10,876 --> 00:17:12,376
Yeah, nice try!

187
00:17:12,376 --> 00:17:14,956
Put those peace shooters on and up to stop me!

188
00:17:15,036 --> 00:17:15,816
You can run!

189
00:21:55,180 --> 00:22:25,160
We'll see you next time.

190
00:22:25,180 --> 00:22:52,580
How many times do I have to tell you?

191
00:22:52,580 --> 00:22:54,060
I'm not coming back!

192
00:22:54,260 --> 00:22:56,600
I don't want to see your faces ever again!

193
00:22:56,800 --> 00:22:57,200
Robin!

194
00:22:57,640 --> 00:22:58,400
Do you hear me?

195
00:22:58,760 --> 00:23:00,700
I just want to die!

196
00:23:00,920 --> 00:23:03,740
Sorry, we're already here and it was a lot of trouble.

197
00:23:04,020 --> 00:23:06,140
So we're gonna go ahead and save you.

198
00:23:06,500 --> 00:23:09,420
On the next One Piece, give us your answer, Robin.

199
00:23:09,740 --> 00:23:11,160
The Straw Hats outcry.

200
00:23:11,160 --> 00:23:13,160
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

